brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net can u compile a list of notable fiction that either a) prophecised smth today correctly! or b) totally missed the mark

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@mortalwombat.info: One type of person I'm getting kind of annoyed by is someone who responds to every story about an AI messing up with "they should've known this would happen. Didn't they ever watch/read [fictional story]?" That's a story! Fiction often explores important ideas and guesses well but it isn't prophecy
